{"arrivo":"sv","origine":"gmw-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-West Germanic","n":6,"n_alternative":5,"parole":[{"parola":"hagga","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"an unpleasant (older) woman; a hag","termine_origine":"*hagatussjā","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*hagatussjā","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately from Proto-West Germanic *hagatussjā (“witch”). Compare häxa (“witch, hag”), a German borrowing."},{"parola":"krubba","pos":"noun|verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps; alternatively","significato":"a manger, a crib, a feeding trough for animals","termine_origine":"*kribbjā","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*kribbjā","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"krubba","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*kribjǭ","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"krübbe","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"osx","nome":"Old Saxon","termine":"kribbia","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*kribbjā","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*kribjǭ","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From Old Swedish krubba, from Old Norse krubba, from Proto-Germanic *kribjǭ. Cognate with German Krippe, English crib. Alternatively, perhaps borrowed from Middle Low German krübbe, kribbe, from Old Saxon kribbia, from Proto-West Germanic *kribbjā, from Proto-Germanic *kribjǭ."},{"parola":"kräkas","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"or from","significato":"to throw up, to vomit","termine_origine":"*krakōn","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*krakōn","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"kræghe","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*krakōn","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*gerh₂-","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*gerg-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From Old Swedish kräkias, from Old Norse kræghe, from Proto-West Germanic *krakōn (“to crack, crackle, shriek”), ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *gerh₂- (“to resound, cry hoarsely”). Cognate with Scots crak (“to crack”), West Frisian kreakje (“to crack”), Dutch kraken (“to crunch, creak, squeak”"},{"parola":"spola","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably; alternatively","significato":"to flush (let water (or another liquid) flow over, usually in order clean, and usually at pressure), (when cleaning) to…","termine_origine":"*spōlijan","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*spōlijan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"spölen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"osx","nome":"Old Saxon","termine":"spōlian","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*spōlijan","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Probably from Middle Low German spölen, from Old Saxon spōlian, from Proto-West Germanic *spōlijan. Compare the older byform spöla. The back vowel could stem from Low German past forms with Rückumlaut. Alternatively it could be from Middle Dutch influence. Cognate with Danish spule, Norwegian Bokmål"},{"parola":"tuta","pos":"noun|verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably; either","significato":"a horn (of a vehicle)","termine_origine":"*þeutan","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*þeutan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"nds","nome":"Low German","termine":"tuten","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"tūten","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*þeutan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From Low German tuten, from Middle Low German tūten, either of imitative origin or derived from Proto-West Germanic *þeutan (“to howl”), itself probably imitative."},{"parola":"ädling","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; alternatively","significato":"a noble (nobleman)","termine_origine":"*aþuling","catena":[{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*aþuling","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"osx","nome":"Old Saxon","termine":"ethiling","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*aþuling","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*aþulingaz","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"ǫðlingr","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Possibly of Middle Low German origin (cf. Middle Low German adel), from Old Saxon ethiling, from Proto-West Germanic *aþuling, from Proto-Germanic *aþulingaz; alternatively from Old Norse ǫðlingr, ultimately from the same Proto-Germanic root."}]}